    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension, improving (I10)</content>. Office 138/84 and home average 136/82, down from 154/90 before treatment but not yet below 130/80; the diuretic&apos;s full effect takes four to six weeks. Sodium 136 and potassium 3.6 mmol/L, both at the low end of normal on hydrochlorothiazide; creatinine 1.02 mg/dL, eGFR 82. Echocardiogram today: no left ventricular hypertrophy, ejection fraction about 60 percent. [S]<list><item>Continue hydrochlorothiazide 25 mg and amlodipine 5 mg; reassess at the next visit before adding or raising a dose.</item><item>Eat potassium-rich fruit and vegetables.</item><item>Electrolytes and a lipid panel at the next visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Asymptomatic right internal carotid stenosis (I65.21)</content>. No symptoms; taking atorvastatin and aspirin without side effects. [S]<list><item>Continue atorvastatin 40 mg and aspirin 81 mg.</item><item>Lipid panel and ALT at the next visit, within 12 weeks of starting.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Office blood pressure, seated, average of two readings</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>138/84 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Home blood pressure monitoring</td><td>At diagnosis and after each treatment change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Average 136/82 over the past week</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium, potassium, creatinine and eGFR</td><td>Baseline; early after starting a diuretic or an ARB; then every 6 months</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sodium 136, potassium 3.6 mmol/L, creatinine 1.02 mg/dL, eGFR 82, four weeks after starting hydrochlorothiazide</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lipid panel</td><td>Baseline; 4 to 12 weeks after starting a statin; then every 3 to 12 months</td><td>Due</td><td>Due at the next visit, ten weeks after starting atorvastatin</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Echocardiogram</td><td>At diagnosis of stage 2 hypertension</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No left ventricular hypertrophy; ejection fraction about 60 percent; mild aortic sclerosis</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Diuretic effects: orthostatic symptoms, cramps, sodium and potassium</td><td>Early after starting, then every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No orthostatic drop; sodium and potassium low-normal</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Antiplatelet adherence and bleeding</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taking aspirin daily; no bleeding or indigestion</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Statin adherence and muscle symptoms</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No muscle symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Stroke warning signs (BE FAST) and calling 911</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No symptoms; knows the signs</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Re-entry social needs: housing, income, benefits, records</td><td>Every visit until settled</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Weekly lease signed; benefits pending</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Office and home blood pressure below 130/80 mmHg by four months. In progress; target 2026-10-27 [S]</item><item>LDL cholesterol lowered by at least half on a statin. In progress; target 2026-09-29 [S]</item><item>Knows the warning signs of stroke and to call 911 at once. Outcome by 2026-07-21: Taught and repeated back the BE FAST signs at the consultation visit [S]</item><item>A stable room, Social Security and Medicare in place, and a health insurance card in hand. In progress; target 2026-09-29 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Hypertension 2025;82:e212-e316) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension, hyperlipidemia and stroke/TIA monographs (2026); 2024 Guideline for the Primary Prevention of Stroke: A Guideline From the American Heart Association/American Stroke Association (Bushnell C, et al. Stroke 2024;55:e344-e424) (2024); 2018 AHA/ACC Guideline on the Management of Blood Cholesterol (Grundy SM, et al. Circulation 2019;139:e1082-e1143) (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Twelve-week review in six weeks, with electrolytes, a lipid panel and ALT. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-29: twelve-week review: blood pressure and lipids after a gout flare on hydrochlorothiazide; switch to losartan. [S]</paragraph></text>

